# tools/recurring-defect-lint.suppressions
#
# Created:  2026-08-08
# Purpose:  The documented, deliberately-frozen residuals that recurring-defect-lint.py
#           would otherwise re-raise on every run. A suppressed finding still prints —
#           as INFO, with the reason below — so nothing disappears silently.
#
# Format:   <path-glob>:<regex>            # reason (must cite an ERR id, a pass, or a
#                                          #  governance rule in CLAUDE.md)
#
# Rules for adding a line: a suppression is a claim that a finding is CORRECT AS IT
# STANDS, not that it is unimportant. If the finding is real but deferred, leave it
# unsuppressed and record it in open-issues.md instead.

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Design supplements frozen at their convergence
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Root CLAUDE.md, "Design supplements": a supplement is frozen at its convergence and
# the section files carry the corrections made after it. All three tables below carry
# the same July-23-2026 promotion-row inversion — the PROMOTED row (v0.3) was written
# and appended before the AR row (v0.2) it records the outcome of, so the pre-promotion
# tail reads v0.1 / v0.3 / v0.2. Rewriting it would rewrite published history.

docs/tracking/injuries-medical-design.md:row v0\.3 is out of order after v0\.1   # CLAUDE.md "Design supplements" — frozen at convergence; the v0.1/v0.3/v0.2 promotion-row order, named in the balance-pass triage list
docs/tracking/training-system-design.md:row v0\.2 is out of order after v0\.1   # same July-23 promotion-row inversion, #29's supplement (frozen at convergence)
docs/tracking/training-system-design.md:row v0\.3 is out of order after v0\.2   # same July-23 promotion-row inversion, #29's supplement (frozen at convergence)
docs/tracking/club-finances-economy-design.md:row v0\.2 is out of order after v0\.3   # same July-23 promotion-row inversion, #40's supplement (frozen at convergence)

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deterministic Sim #16 §3.5 — the two v1.0.14 rows
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two independent approval-wave back-props (ERR-043-001 at #43's approval, July 24;
# ERR-045-001 at #45's approval, July 25) each added the same three reserved-ordinal
# placeholder rows and each recorded itself as v1.0.14. Left as found: renumbering
# either row would break the citations in #43's and #45's own approval records.

docs/specs/deterministic-sim/section-3.md:duplicate version row v1\.0\.14   # two July-24/25 approval-wave back-props (ERR-043-001, ERR-045-001) collided on one patch number; left as found

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRE-ARMED — documented residuals the current scan scope does not reach
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# These match nothing today, deliberately. Class 2's population is docs/specs/**/*.md
# plus docs/tracking/*-design.md, so the CHANGELOG tables are out of scope; the rules
# are here so that widening the scope does not re-raise a collision the project has
# already decided to leave alone. CHANGELOG-src.md v2.80 and v2.85 record both.

docs/tracking/CHANGELOG-src.md:duplicate version row v2\.79   # CHANGELOG-src v2.80: two concurrent Aug-7 sessions (ERR-008-023 and client P5a) both took 2.79 — left as found per the no-edit rule
docs/tracking/CHANGELOG-src.md:duplicate version row v2\.8[234]   # CHANGELOG-src v2.85: 2.82-2.84 were already in the table from the T2 review rounds when the chain's entry took 2.81 — left as found per the no-edit rule
docs/specs/season-competition-loop/section-3.md:duplicate version row v0\.7 # ERR-030-022: ERR-030-007 was filed twice (#42's and #32's approvals) — the duplicate rows ARE the record of the double-filing §3.3.1 reconciles; renumbering breaks both approval records
docs/specs/season-competition-loop/section-3.md:duplicate version row v0\.8 # ERR-030-022: same — ERR-030-008/-009 (#45) and ERR-030-009 (#44) each took v0.8; the reconciliation is §3.3.1, the rows stay as filed
